    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Bryce Harper** serving as the clear anchor of the lineup, boasting an elite 80.21 score against Mikolas. The combination of an elite matchup against a pitcher with a 4.77 xERA and a significant 8% boost from strong BvP history makes him our must-start anchor. Alongside him, **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53) provide excellent value; **Dylan Beavers** is particularly well-positioned as he benefits from an optimal leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Johnson, while **Luis Arraez** maintains his high floor through consistent contact profile and favorable park factors. **Jeremiah Jackson** (68.45) also rounds out the top tier of our starting group, finding a high ceiling in a favorable matchup against a struggling Johnson.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision today involved **Braden Montgomery**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 39.77 score. Despite strong park factors, the combination of a tough matchup against Suarez (3.55 xERA) and a lower-order placement pushed him just below our 40.0 efficiency floor, leading us to bench him to preserve our game caps. Meanwhile, we are closely monitoring the bottom of our order; **Justin Crawford** (65.19) remains a strong play despite hitting 9th, as his elite sprint speed gives us the SB upside we desperately need in a 5x5 format. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (56.73), whose score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite catcher and a high-caliber arm in McLean, though his pedigree keeps him in the starting nine. We continue to manage the health of **Will Smith** and **Cal Raleigh**, who remain unavailable, keeping our catching depth restricted.",
